      "side": 1,
      "message": "Splitting the following suggestion into its own thread ([source](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/2812620/comment/a09e87e5_db4b3eb5/)):\n\n\u003e What about treating pvIOMMUs as another special set of assigned devices by introducing `DeviceAssignmentInfo::(assigned_)pviommus: BTreeSet\u003cu32\u003e` of `id`? You\u0027d get the uniqueness check in the ctor for free and could [patch the template pvIOMMU nodes by iterating through `self.assigned_pviommus`]\n\nRegarding your question:\n\n\u003e\u003e This will break once we extend the topology to multiple devices per pvIOMMU.\n\u003e\n\u003e I\u0027m sorry but could you elaborate details when would my code break?\n\nImagine running your current code on\n```\n/{\n    a { \u003ciommus\u003e \u003d \u003c\u0026pviommu\u003e; }\n    b { \u003ciommus\u003e \u003d \u003c\u0026pviommu\u003e; }\n    pviommu: ... { ... }\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 290,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 290,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "5d139c8977760880bd085ba389ff95ec88f08576",
