      "writtenOn": "2023-11-16T16:12:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Removed L359. Thank you for spotting this.\n\n\nRe clean-up: I think that pvmfw is already cleaning up and sanitizing DT nodes to ensure everything are under pvmfw\u0027s control. I thought that that\u0027s why we\u0027re patching platform DT instead of having lots of validation checks. Am I misunderstanding?\n\nActually I\u0027m doing this just because of one tricky case. If pvmfw got 12 PV IOMMUs while only 9 are assigned for real, then we\u0027ll fail to boot because we only have 10 pre-populated PV IOMMUs for patching. I maybe worrying too much for low possibility case, but I just wanted to do best effort. What do you think?\n\nIf you think that it\u0027s too much, then I can do one of following (which I think that it\u0027s cleaner)\n  - Option 1) `parse_iommus()` to return `(BTreeSet\u003cPvIommu\u003e, BTreeMap\u003cPhandle, PvIommu\u003e)` and keep `BTreeSet` in `DeviceAssignmentInfo` without modification.\n  - Option 2) Simply generates `iommu_ids` with `BTreeMap\u003cPhandle, PvIommu\u003e::values()` outside of `parse_iommus()`.",
      "parentUuid": "c895b152_537617bd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 290,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 290,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "5d139c8977760880bd085ba389ff95ec88f08576",
